:name: NUCLEO-H743ZI2
:description: Runs a firmware ELF on Renode's Nucleo-144 H7 model; the ST-LINK console (USART3) is logged.
:  Used by `make sim` / `make sim-live`. Manual use:
:  renode --console --disable-gui -e 'set elf @out/hello_hw.elf; include @renode/nucleo_h743zi2.resc; start'

using sysbus

$elf ?= @out/hello_hw.elf
$repl ?= @renode/nucleo_h743zi2.repl

mach create "nucleo_h743zi2"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $repl

showAnalyzer sysbus.usart3 Antmicro.Renode.Analyzers.LoggingUartAnalyzer

# Runs at start-up and on every machine reset (e.g. an IWDG reset).
macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $elf
    # Renode doesn't model GPIO pull-ups: hold the active-low break input
    # (PE15) at its idle level, as the pull-up does on the real board.
    sysbus.gpioPortE OnGPIO 15 true
"""
runMacro $reset
